        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The further challenge is Judgment and Order dated 10.08.2011 passed by the learned Sessions Judge, Cachar at Silchar in Criminal Appeal No. 24/2009, whereby the learned Appellate Court dismissed the appeal and upheld the conviction."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f063fa9bf1d74ab4a946004e2aad0385_7",
        "summary_section": "facts",
        "labels": [
          "RLC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_labels:RLC"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n3. Referring to the decision of the Hon'ble Apex Court in the case of M/s A.K.Sarkar & Co. & Anr.\n-Vs- The State of West Bengal & Ors reported in 2024 INSC 186 , Mr. Bora, learned Senior Counsel for the petitioners argues that the sentence"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8ca22bd1627646d8b4027601958b0b07_15",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Perused the materials available on record including the provisions of Act, 1954 and the Act, 2006."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3d7fdd1a531b4976a9085c54328970da_16",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n6. Section 7 of the Act, 1954 prohibits any person to manufacture for sale or store, sell or to distribute any adulterated food and any misbranded food etc.\n7."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d35de13781ea4c2581b1ecb63885fd93_17",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The allegation in the complaint as well as the conviction under Section 7 of the Act, 1954 of the petitioners herein, is relatable to adulteration and misbranding."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8a7e1d169770496685ecc85657ac2de7_18",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "8. The Act, 2006 was enacted with an object to consolidate the laws relating to food and to establish the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India for laying down science based standards for articles of food and to regulate their manufa"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "afc2dd8e52664398bb2cd94a6cfb872f_19",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In terms of Section 97 of the Act, 2006, the Acts/Orders specified in Second Schedule were repealed, which include the Act, 1954."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "249b6fa4841840b1873b67fb038f3f24_20",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Clause-(ii) of Sub Section 1 of Section 97 of the Act, 2006"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8a100a8f46654acc8867e2f61d224bef_21",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "on the other hand prescribes that such repeal shall not affect any right, privilege application or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under any of the enactment or orders under repeal."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b756c3a79f9844918ea3d1c1ea4c1ba9_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "10. That being the position, generally the repeal of Act, 1954 shall not have any affect on the conviction made in the case in hand under the Act, 1954."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f344f3b648924810a0eb35983e776665_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "However, the Hon'ble Apex Court in Trilok Chand -Vs- State of Himachal Pradesh reported in 2020 10 SCC 763 referring to the earlier judgment of the Hon'ble Apex Court in T. Barai -Vs- Henry Ah Hoe reported in (1983) 1 SCC 177,\nmore particul"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "617a4fa66dfa403e8cf7aa47935bebaf_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "12. Section 51 of the Act, 2006 prescribes that any person who, whether by himself or by any other person on his behalf manufactures for sale or stores or sells or distributes or imports any article of food for human consumption which is su"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fd9748e1d8544a538fe5667b49a3c7c4_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the case in hand, the complaint and the conviction is also relatable to an allegation which says that the material/food seized from the possession of the accused petitioners were adulterated."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "39a09a899e9c43a29f209eaf8b61703a_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, learned counsel, in the considered opinion of this Court, is correct in arguing that such conviction is relatable to Section 51 of the Act, 2006."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7299c94d3ea54f37a265d93344c3bf44_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "13. Therefore, in the given context of the present case, this Court is of the view that the determination made in Trilok Chand (supra) and M/s A.K.Sarkar (supra) can be made applicable to the facts of the present case."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0c070b53cee1494eabe09d61f306a84f_29",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "14. Accordingly, the present criminal revision petition stands allowed by interfering with the sentence of Simple Imprisonment for 6 (six) months each and it is directed that the sentence be confined to the fine already directed to be paid."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "276ff87ea95f43e2b3959fa31934b38e_30",
        "summary_section": "decision",
